<title>UK: Wessex Water H1 pretax profit up 10 pct.</title>
<headline>Wessex Water H1 pretax profit up 10 pct.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1996-12-03</dateline>
<text>
<p>Six months ending September 30</p>
<p>			   (million stg unless stated)</p>
<p> Shr (pence) (diluted)  22.1		   vs 20.1</p>
<p> Dividend (pence)	 5.7		    vs 5.0</p>
<p> Pretax		     75.5		   vs 68.4</p>
<p> Turnover		   128.9		  vs 120.3</p>
<p>NOTE - Analysts had forecast pre-tax profits in a range between 72 and 77 million stg.</p>
<p>Full company name - Wessex Water Plc  </p>
<p> Operating result	 67.0		   vs 59.9</p>
<p> Interest		   2.3 receivable     vs 2.5 receivable</p>
<p> Tax			  12.4		   vs 10.5</p>
<p> Attributable	     63.1		   vs 57.9</p>
<p> Retained profit	  46.0		   vs 46.2</p>
<p>Note - Wessex Water Plc is a water and sewerage company.</p>
<p>-- London Newsroom +44 171 5427717</p>
</text>
